  "description": "We need to replace and increase the current storage facilities we have at the bowls club site. The current storage is a 8ft x 10ft foot metal container that is in the wooded area on the south side of the bowling greens. The reasons are as follows:\n- The current metal storage container has several holes within the steel frame and therefore is not water tight.\n- The current metal container is placed directly on the grass surface and so damp has rotted the interior floor timbers, which is dangerous to walk on.\n- Any replacement metal container could not go into the current location ,due to access, without cutting down or disturbing several large mature trees plus surrounding shrubs.\n-The Bexley Council Park management looked at the current site and advised that the new position proposed in this application was the best location.\n-We need to increase the amount of storage space and so are requesting a 8ft x 20 ft replacement metal container.\n- To facilitate the position of the new metal container suitable concrete corner pillars will be provided for support.\n-The reason for the increase in storage is that the current green keeping fees expenditure we are paying means the club is making a significant financial loss each year, which is unsustainable.\n-The solution to this issue is that we follow what every other bowls club in L B of Bexley does and manage our own green keeping.\n-In order to manage this work then the bowls club will need to purchase the equipment necessary for us to be able to do this.\n-We need a safe and sucure place to keep the equipment.\n-Equipment to be stored would include 2-3 mowers used to cut the grass surrounding the greens. A high quality cylinder mower to cut the actual greens, a second mower with a set of cartridges for green work (Scarifier, thatch remover, verticutter, sarel roller & brush), a roller, a slitter, sprayer, spreader plus other maintenance equipment, shelving and fertiliser storage.          ",
